# Normalise line endings in the repository, not in each contributor's editor.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone that checks out CRLF produces a diff on every
# line of every file, and the formatter reports the whole tree as changed. The
# working tree keeps the platform's native endings; what Git stores, and what CI
# checks out, is always LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are captured evidence and are hashed by `test/replay.test.ts`. They
# are already LF; pinning them means no checkout can silently rewrite them.
test/fixtures/** -text

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary

# Keep the generated bundle out of diffs and language statistics.
#
# Only `index.js` is generated — by `vp pack`. `lib/client.js` sits beside it and
# is hand-written, so marking it generated would hide real changes from review.
lib/index.js linguist-generated=true
